# Dependencies
node_modules/

# The npm lockfile, if one is ever generated. `bun.lock` is the one that is committed -- two
# lockfiles for one dependency tree is how a resolution difference between developers happens.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Next.js build output
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Fumadocs' generated MDX index. Rebuilt from source.config.ts on every build.
.source/

# The docs copied out of each mod repository by scripts/sync.mjs are NOT ignored -- see the note
# under `apps/docs/content/` in AGENT.md. It is the one generated tree this repository carries, so
# that the documentation is readable here as well as on the site. The mods are still the only place
# a page is written: the sync wipes the tree and rebuilds it on every build, and `check.mjs` refuses
# a build whose regenerated tree differs from what is committed. Do not add a rule for it here.

# Copied out of the root by sync.mjs, because Next cannot import from outside its own directory.
apps/docs/manifest.json
apps/docs/glossary.json

# NOT ignored, deliberately, and there are two different reasons in this folder.
#
# apps/docs/public/site/ holds the site's two marks — one per theme, and the source for the tab icon and
# the OG card. They are copied BY HAND from aaenz/public/assets/logo-mark*.png, because no build step can
# fetch them and no transform could reproduce them: the files ARE the drawing. The folder also holds
# portrait.png, the masthead's image, which IS generated — by `bun run portrait` from
# design/portrait-source/. check.mjs asserts the marks' geometry and ink, the portrait's transparent
# ground and footprint, that the tab's <link>s name the pair, and that the build copied each through
# unchanged — everything short of reaching that other repository.
#
# apps/docs/public/icons/ and apps/docs/public/brand/ ARE generated — by `bun run icons` from
# design/icons-source/ and `bun run brand` from design/brand-source/ — and committed anyway, because the
# build reads them at render time to inline them. A deploy that ran the transform first could differ from
# what was reviewed. The sources are committed too, so both transforms are reproducible, and check.mjs
# asserts that neither pair has drifted apart.

# Fetched from Modrinth and CurseForge by scripts/stats.mjs on every build. Generated, so not
# committed -- a committed copy is a download count that was true on the day somebody built.
apps/docs/stats.json

# THERE WAS AN `apps/docs/public/avatar.*` LINE HERE. It is gone with the avatar it retired: the
# masthead's image is a committed file now — the portrait under public/site/ — nothing downloads a profile
# picture at build time, and an ignore rule for that name would be the only thing left of it.


# The pinned-commit checkouts sync.mjs makes when a mod's folder is not present. One per mod, each a
# bare snapshot at the SHA in manifest.json. Reproducible from the manifest and safe to delete.
.cache/

# Build logs and captured command output. Written by `bun run dev` and by redirecting a build to a file
# while checking something; never something to commit, and always regenerable.
*.log
*.out.txt

# PLANNED MODS, AND EVERY IDEA IN THEM. A mod that is not certain to exist is not named on the site --
# not in the catalog, not as a served icon, not in the bundle a visitor downloads -- and it is not named
# in this repository either, because a name, a role and a one-line summary ARE the idea. So the entries
# deferred out of `manifest.json`, the plan for them, and their icon sources all live under here.
#
# This is the arrangement the mod repositories already use for their own `plan.md`: the working document
# is on disk and out of git. Promote an entry into `manifest.json` and its icon into
# `design/icons-source/` the day the mod is certain; `design/planned/suite.json` says how.
design/planned/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
